Z||000009||ChadMan||03-19-2000||10:47 AM||||I've seen a Miata "low-profile headlight" conversion (I confess - I like Miatas) where they use the factory headlight doors, but replace the big round headlamp with small round ones.  The headlights only pop up about three inches.  See it here:  <A HREF="http://www.miata.net/motm/2000/dailey.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.miata.net/motm/2000/dailey.html</A> <P>Wonder if something similar could be finagled for the Fiero - maybe using the small rectangular lights from early 4th-gen Camaros?||||reg||1
Z||000010||TOM||03-19-2000||02:29 PM||||The Kits I have available are also have a clear acrylic cover available. The camaro light bulbs are just a smidgen too wide to fit them in the opening of a fiero light door||||reg||1
