Z||000012||ChadMan||03-19-2000||05:53 PM||||Yes, Lawrence!  Is that your car?  That's EXACTLY what I had in mind.  Those look incredibly cool.  You'd have no hi-beams, though, would you?  I guess you could make up for that with driving lights.<P>Damn, that's cool.||||reg||10
Z||000013||lawrence||03-19-2000||07:18 PM||||Yes, I have high beams.  These are home made light fixtures.  Well, modified headlights, really.  I took the single filament halogen tube out of a 4351 headlamp and installed a 9007 dual filament lamp, in a standard bayonet socket.  So, these are now replaceable type fixtures.<P>I put a physical stop on the lever arm to limit the stroke of the doors.  Since this is an 88, the headlight motor controllers read stall current and quit when they hit the stops.  You can just barely see the doors from the driver's seat.<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe</A>  - WebElectric Magazine||||reg||1
Z||000014||VISCERAL||03-20-2000||12:24 PM||||Lawrence, could you please give us some more info, or if you could be so kind as to put a web page on your website regarding your awesome light modification. Thanks, Patrick||||reg||14
Z||000015||lawrence||03-20-2000||10:26 PM||||I'm not sure if I'll ever publish an article about these, but I did put together a quick description of what I did.  See it here:<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe/other/fiero/lowprofile.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe/other/fiero/lowprofile.htm</A> <P>Have fun,<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe</A>  - WebElectric Magazine||||reg||1
